      "text": "⚠️ If you shine a laser at an AMO aircraft, you WILL be caught and prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law!\n\nMeet 2 recent Oregon offenders who didn't get the memo 👇\n\n🔴Brian Keith Kapileo Nepaial, 38, of Aloha, Oregon, was charged October 16, with pointing a laser at an AMO helicopter and possessing methamphetamine with the intent to distribute.\n\n🔴Hector Miranda-Mendoza, 35, unlawfully living in Oregon, was charged October 3, with the felony offense of aiming a laser pointer at an aircraft.\n\n⚠️Reminder: Aiming a laser at an aircraft is punishable by up to five years in federal prison and/or a fine of up to $250,000.",
